# Wave W17-X (Route 212 — North): reed post — a reed marker post where the path gives up: a weathered post with a single cattail standing at its shoulder, marking the last dry footing before the pools take the road (design: boardwalk sections starting where the path gives up in the painting — no boardwalk kind ships on the segment maps; the posts carry the giving-up instead). On pool turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 212 — South’s lily posts by the cattail entire: the North marks footing, the South marks water.
